   "note": "Design uses a translation-invariant ansatz block to match the cyclic topology of the input sites (0-1-2-3-4-5-0). The block consists of a layer of parameterized RY rotations, followed by a ring of CNOTs, a layer of parameterized RZ rotations, and a second ring of CNOTs. The CNOT rings are fixed structure (no params) and are invariant under cyclic permutation of qubits. The rotation layers use distinct parameters per site, but the block structure itself (gate types and connectivity) is invariant under the cyclic shift generator. This allows the model to learn site-specific features while respecting the underlying symmetry of the feature map if it is also cyclic, or simply providing a structured, low-risk connectivity pattern that avoids the barren plateaus often seen in fully connected random ansatzes. The hypothesis claims invariance under cyclic permutation, which is a strong structural prior for ring-like data.",
